title: $:/mf/gen/CLI command/mf repo calibrate-threshold
catalog: CLI command
target: mf repo calibrate-threshold
summary: Measure the mass-write thresholds of the selected repository's disk

!! Reference

```
Measure the mass-write thresholds of the selected repository's disk

On a throwaway store beside the repository's, removed afterwards, each kind of write (add, remove, set, delete) to N records is timed one record at a time and in bulk, cold, for N = 4, 8, 16, 32…: a kind's threshold is the most records written one at a time before going in bulk is past 250 ms one at a time and three times quicker (doc "Calibrating the mass-write thresholds"). Takes minutes on a hard disk; the repository stays usable meanwhile.

Usage: mf repo calibrate-threshold [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --records <RECORDS>
          Records of the throwaway store
          
          [default: 100000]

      --write
          Write the thresholds found into the repository's config.json, in force at once

      --json
          Print the daemon's answer as JSON

      --poll-interval <MS>
          Poll interval in ms while waiting

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
```
